## Why This Is Asked
Tests depth in distributed systems patterns (Saga, Event Sourcing, CQRS) and practical orchestration with compensations.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration vs choreography
- Idempotency and deduplication
- Compensating actions and failure handling
- Snapshotting and read-model strategies
- Event versioning and replay

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal saga state machine
const Saga = { state: 'Created', steps: [] };
function apply(event) {
  switch(event.type) {
    case 'InventoryReserved': Saga.state = 'InventoryReserved'; break;
    case 'PaymentInitiated': Saga.state = 'PaymentPending'; break;
    case 'PaymentConfirmed': Saga.state = 'Paid'; break;
    case 'Shipped': Saga.state = 'Shipped'; break;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle idempotent retries for PaymentFailed?
- What strategies for event versioning and schema evolution do you recommend?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of token binding and multi-idp flows in production.

## Key Concepts
- Token binding with cnf
- per-tenant key rotation
- KMS/JWK management
- auditing and revocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Issuer (simplified)
const tenantKwk = getTenantKey(tenantId); // {kid, jwk}
const token = jwt.sign({sub, iss: 'gateway', aud: tenantAud}, tenantPrivateKey, { algorithm:'ES256', header: { kid: tenantKwk.kid }, nonce: crypto.randomBytes(16).toString('hex'), cnf: { jwk: tenantKwk.jwk } });

// Verifier
const decoded = jwt.verify(token, tenantPublicKey, { algorithms:['ES256'] });
if (!compareJwk(decoded.cnf.jwk, getTenantBoundJwk(tenantId))) throw new Error('binding mismatch');
